%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: ef4120e8d7cc4784ba80e7aeb2d6d58d, type: 3}
  m_Name: Bragi_Ending_Death
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  Repeatable: 0
  Lines:
  - Text: 'Oftentimes, stories have no audience. That is what I devoted my life to;
      telling those stories. Our most beautiful lie was to be one of those stories. '
    Speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 221624e13721edf47a3982f9e2ec5bd5, type: 2}
  - Text: 'Born of poison and blood, the Child of Lies faced challenges three and
      even struck down the storyteller, who broke his oath to try to stop the subject
      of his story. Ah, the beauty of it all. '
    Speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 221624e13721edf47a3982f9e2ec5bd5, type: 2}
  - Text: "I weep at the thought of what might come next. I reckon\u2026 the little
      Lie enters the cave where the Father of Lies is trapped, and in the presence
      of his saviour, the chains break."
    Speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 221624e13721edf47a3982f9e2ec5bd5, type: 2}
  - Text: Loki falls to the ground, and Sigyn is there to catch him. The pair weeps,
      and the Lie falls to their knees as they are overwhelmed by the sight.
    Speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 221624e13721edf47a3982f9e2ec5bd5, type: 2}
  - Text: Thank you, newborn child, for saving us.
    Speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: f4f22446a67128b49b991b6336d3fa9a, type: 2}
  - Text: '*Unintelligible*'
    Speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 90eaea05785be1045b412500bff1817a, type: 2}
  - Text: "Father, mother\u2026 I am back."
    Speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8b9b771dc2f105a40a7ee49c43e5d895, type: 2}
  - Text: I wonder, would Sigyn and Loki open their arms to let this child into their
      family, or would they be scorned, considered a facsimile of the children Loki
      truly lost.
    Speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 221624e13721edf47a3982f9e2ec5bd5, type: 2}
  - Text: Oh, child, I am sorry for having forced this trial upon you. We love you
      so for the freedom you have brought us.
    Speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: f4f22446a67128b49b991b6336d3fa9a, type: 2}
  - Text: "Yes, I do not believe Sigyn could ever reject a child in front of her,
      she is too loving for that. Loki might be broken by the torture, but he would
      recover and speak in due time, I\u2019m sure."
    Speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 221624e13721edf47a3982f9e2ec5bd5, type: 2}
  - Text: "You\u2026 you are not my Fenrir or my Hel. I see\u2026 you\u2026 child
      of mine\u2026"
    Speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 90eaea05785be1045b412500bff1817a, type: 2}
  - Text: 'Yes, I believe that is how this story goes on. '
    Speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 221624e13721edf47a3982f9e2ec5bd5, type: 2}
  - Text: "Ah, if only I had not been killed. I would have loved to see Ragnar\xF6k
      too, for the story that ends the world must be the most beautiful one."
    Speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 221624e13721edf47a3982f9e2ec5bd5, type: 2}
  - Text: 'Little Lie, when the end comes by your hand, will you tell the world that
      you set its demise into action, or will you try to defy unbreakable prophecy? '
    Speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 221624e13721edf47a3982f9e2ec5bd5, type: 2}
  - Text: Thus, the third act begins.
    Speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 221624e13721edf47a3982f9e2ec5bd5, type: 2}
  OnFinished:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
